# Kanban Board Maintenance (for Cursor Agent)

GOAL

- Treat `## Registry` as the single source of truth. `## Board` is always derived from it.
- Only perform the allowed operations below; never free-form edit the Board.

ALLOWED OPERATIONS

1) ADD_CARD: Add to `## Registry` with required fields (ID, Title, Status, Assignee, Links, Notes).
2) MOVE_CARD: Change `Status` in `## Registry` only; then regenerate the `## Board` section from `## Registry`.
3) EDIT_CARD: Update fields in `## Registry`; then regenerate `## Board`.
4) ARCHIVE_CARD: Move cards with `Status: Done` older than 7 days to `## Archive` (append-only).
5) RENDER_BOARD: Rebuild the whole `## Board` from `## Registry`.

RENDERING RULES

- Columns: Backlog | Doing | Review | Done (in that order).
- Each card shows: `[ID] Title — Assignee` on one line; links on the next line (optional).
- Do not drop metadata from the Registry when rendering the Board.
- If a card lacks an ID, generate one like `K-YYYYMMDD-###`.

CHECKS BEFORE COMMIT

- Ensure unique IDs in `## Registry`.
- Ensure every card has a `Status` that matches one of the Board columns.
- Rebuild `## Board` 1:1 from `## Registry` (no manual edits inside `## Board`).

EDITING PROTOCOL

- Apply operations to `## Registry` first.
- Only then run RENDER_BOARD to refresh `## Board`.
- Leave `## Instructions for AI Agents` untouched except when explicitly asked.

AUDIT TRAIL

- Add a short "Changelog" subsection at the bottom with bullet points:
  - `YYYY-MM-DD [AgentName]: OPERATION details...`
